            "review_text": "kaykaysmith\n40 contributions\n0\nDon’t go individually - tourist destination for groups\nMar 2019 • Family\nWe went here at the recommendation of our guide (which they didn’t know or maybe they would have provided better service if they’d known a tour organization would get the feedback). The building was lovely but as a couple we were seated next to a large tour group with the guide giving instructions on luggage, etc. The service was terrible and rude - no explaination of the extensive menu, just “what do you want”. I assume this is because they are used to groups and pre-arranged meals that are already decided on. Once the group left we got a little more service but then 2 guide escorted couples came on either side of us and they were fawned over while we were ignored. As we left we noticed every room filled with groups. We were considering dessert but when no one returned to take our order for 15 minutes we decided we wanted out of there and it took quite an effort to get the attention of anyone to get our bill. Then we were oddly escorted downstairs to pay the bill like we were in trouble. The worst meal experience of 3 weeks in Indochina. \nOur guide the next day was surprised as he said it had been good in the past but he would take it off their referral list.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten March 26, 2019",
